  <section class="ky-section" id="ky-features">
    <div class="ky-container">
      <div class="ky-section-header">
        <span class="ky-eyebrow">Technology Made Human</span>
        <h2 class="ky-accent-heading">What the KOYO 303TS Actually Does For You</h2>
        <p>Great massage chair technology disappears into the experience. These are not features to be impressed by — they are the reasons the 303TS feels the way it does when you are actually sitting in it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border:1px solid var(--ky-border);border-radius:var(--ky-radius-xl);overflow:hidden">
        <div class="ky-features-grid">
          <div class="ky-feat-panel"><div class="ky-feat-num">01 — MECHANISM</div><h3>Servo 4D: Where the Feel Actually Lives</h3><p>The 4D designation means the massage mechanism moves in four dimensions: up-down, side-to-side, in-out depth, and speed variation. But the word "servo" changes everything. Servo-controlled movement means the mechanism responds to programmed variation with genuine precision — depth increases are measured and controlled, not mechanical approximations. Combined with the anthropoid silicone heads, the result is massage movement that feels intentional and organic rather than mechanical and repetitive.</p></div>
          <div class="ky-feat-panel"><div class="ky-feat-num">02 — CONTACT POINTS</div><h3>Anthropoid Silicone Heads: Engineered for Human Feel</h3><p>Most massage chair roller heads are rigid spheres. The 303TS uses silicone massage heads shaped to mimic the geometry of a real hand's thumb and knuckle: firm in the center for pressure, softly compliant at the edges for natural transition. This means contact with your spine, shoulder blades, and neck feels graduated rather than blunt — a subtle engineering choice with a very direct effect on how the massage feels.</p></div>
          <div class="ky-feat-panel"><div class="ky-feat-num">03 — TRACK SYSTEM</div><h3>Hybrid SL-Track: Coverage Without Dead Zones</h3><p>The hybrid SL-Track follows the natural double-curve of your spine — first the S-curve from your neck through your lumbar vertebrae, then the L-extension into the upper hamstring area. This continuous path means the roller does not stop at your tailbone and leave the most stress-carrying muscles of the hip untouched. When combined with zero gravity recline, the contact is maintained across the full track length without loss of pressure.</p></div>
          <div class="ky-feat-panel"><div class="ky-feat-num">04 — PERSONALIZATION</div><h3>Auto Body Scan: Your Session, Shaped to You</h3><p>Before any massage program begins, the 303TS scans you. It measures your shoulder height and spine dimensions, then calculates a roller path that matches your actual body profile. For buyers who share the chair with a partner of different height or build, the auto scan means both users get a personalized experience — not one that represents a compromise.</p></div>
          <div class="ky-feat-panel"><div class="ky-feat-num">05 — RECLINE &amp; HEAT</div><h3>Zero Gravity + Heat: The Difference Between Relaxed and Deeply Relaxed</h3><p>Zero gravity recline positions your body so your knees are slightly elevated above your heart, redistributing your weight and reducing compressive force on your spinal discs. Sessions in zero gravity feel noticeably deeper — the same intensity setting delivers more decompression because your skeleton is no longer fighting gravity. Layer in calf and low back heat, and the muscles begin loosening before the massage intensity needs to work for it.</p></div>
          <div class="ky-feat-panel"><div class="ky-feat-num">06 — FULL BODY &amp; AUDIO</div><h3>Air Massage, Foot Rollers &amp; Bluetooth: A Complete Session</h3><p>Full-body air compression wraps the arms, shoulders, seat, hips, legs, and feet in programmed compression cycles — enhancing circulation and contributing a satisfying sense of total physical engagement. Foot rollers work the soles with rolling and kneading motion. The Bluetooth sound system connects your phone seamlessly, letting you use the chair as a multi-sensory decompression experience during every session.</p></div>
