  {%- comment -%} FAQ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ky-section ky-section-warm" id="ky-faq">
    <div class="ky-container-narrow">
      <div class="ky-section-header">
        <span class="ky-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</span>
        <h2 class="ky-accent-heading">Everything You Need to Know About KOYO</h2>
        <p>Real buyer questions, answered thoroughly and honestly. If your question is not here, call or email us directly — our specialists are happy to help.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ky-faq-list">
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What makes KOYO massage chairs different from other brands at this price?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>KOYO's primary differentiation is its combination of made-in-Japan manufacturing with a comfort-first engineering philosophy. The Servo 4D system with anthropoid silicone massage heads is meaningfully different from standard massage chair rollers — the heads flex like thumbs and knuckles rather than rolling as rigid spheres, which translates into a more natural, organic contact feel. The precision brushless motor runs quieter and longer than standard brushed motors. Auto body scan personalization means the chair adjusts to your body profile, not an average template.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>Is the KOYO 303TS actually made in Japan?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>Yes. The KOYO 303TS is manufactured in Japan. The brand's identity is built around Japanese manufacturing standards, comfort-first engineering, and long-term reliability. Japan's production culture emphasizes precision and consistency — which translates into a chair that sounds, moves, and feels premium through years of daily use.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What is the Servo 4D mechanism and how is it different from regular 4D?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>The 4D designation means the massage mechanism moves in four dimensions: up-down, side-to-side, in-out depth, and speed variation. The word "servo" changes everything. Servo-controlled movement means the mechanism responds to programmed variation with genuine precision — depth increases are measured and controlled, not mechanical approximations. Combined with anthropoid silicone heads, the result is massage movement that feels intentional and organic rather than mechanical and repetitive.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What colors does the KOYO 303TS come in and what are the differences?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>The KOYO 303TS is available in three genuine finish options — all with identical performance: Black (the most versatile, works in any interior style), Pearl (bright and modern, ideal for white walls, light oak, or Scandinavian interiors), and Walnut (warm, grounded, with wood accent tones — reads as furniture in classic or warm-toned rooms). The choice is purely aesthetic.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What are the size and weight recommendations for the KOYO 303TS?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>The KOYO 303TS is designed for users between 5'0" and 6'0" tall, with a maximum recommended user weight of 265 lbs (120 kg). For buyers outside this range, our specialists can recommend alternative models that may better fit your dimensions — visit our showroom or call for guidance.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>Can I try the KOYO 303TS before buying?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>Absolutely — and we strongly recommend it. The difference between reading about the Servo 4D mechanism and anthropoid silicone heads, and actually feeling a session with them, is substantial. Our showroom carries the KOYO 303TS available for guided demos. Call {{ section.settings.phone | default: '+1 (408) 889-1188' }} to schedule a visit or book an appointment online.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>Do you offer financing for the KOYO 303TS?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>Yes — we offer financing through Affirm, which splits the purchase into manageable monthly payments with transparent terms. Rates and approval depend on your situation. Contact us for details, or check terms during checkout.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="ky-faq-item"><div class="ky-faq-q" onclick="kyToggleFaq(this)"><h3>How long does delivery take and what does white-glove delivery include?</h3><span class="ky-faq-toggle">+</span></div><div class="ky-faq-a"><div class="ky-faq-a-inner"><p>In-stock KOYO 303TS models typically ship within 5–14 business days via white-glove delivery nationwide. This means delivery to the room of your choice, fully assembled placement, and a test-before-we-leave guarantee. Timelines may vary by region. Contact us at {{ section.settings.phone | default: '+1 (408) 889-1188' }} for current availability.</p></div></div></div>
